   <div class="PGHDR" style="text-align: left; width: 100%">
    <div class="hf-row">
     <div class="hf-cell TOCLink">
       &#160;
     </div>
    </div>
   </div>
  </div>
  <p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: left">&#160;</p>
  <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt 15pt 0pt 51pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0pt;">We utilize commodity derivative instruments primarily to attempt to mitigate the effect of commodity price volatility&#160;and to provide greater certainty of cash flows associated with sales of our commodities. We utilize mark-to-market accounting to account for these instruments. Thus, our results in any given period can be impacted,&#160;sometimes significantly, by changes in market prices relative to our contract price along with the timing of the valuation change in the derivative instruments relative to the sale of biofuel. We include the mark-to-market or non-cash portion of&#160;this item as an adjustment to adjusted EBITDA&#160;as we believe it provides a relevant indicator of the underlying performance of our business in a given period.</p>
  <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:55pt;margin-right:18.45pt;margin-top:0pt;text-align:justify;">&#160;</p>
  <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt 15pt 0pt 51pt; text-align: justify;">The following table reconciles net&#160;income (loss), the most directly comparable GAAP performance financial measure, with adjusted EBITDA.&#160;</p>
